# Live/rescue medium convenience — liveuser is wheel + NOPASSWD here since
# this is a removable disk with an unset (locked) account password, not a
# hardened install. Reassess before this convention carries over to an
# installed system in phase 4.
#
# Filename prefixed zz- deliberately: sudo reads /etc/sudoers.d/* in
# lexicographic order and the LAST matching rule for a user wins. Without
# the prefix this sorted as "liveuser" < "wheel", so sudoers.d/wheel's
# password-required %wheel rule (needed for real installed users) silently
# overrode this NOPASSWD grant for liveuser too, since liveuser is also in
# the wheel group — confirmed live: Calamares' own launch line (`sudo env
# ... calamares`, no TTY available in a sway exec context) failed outright
# with "a password is required" and Calamares never appeared, on a build
# that otherwise booted and logged in fine. zz- sorts after "wheel",
# restoring the intended precedence.
%wheel ALL=(ALL:ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL
